     rraaddiiuussdd — Remote Authentication Dial In User Service (RADIUS) daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     rraaddiiuussdd [--ddnn] [--ff _f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rraaddiiuussdd daemon implements the RADIUS protocol.

     To have rraaddiiuussdd enabled at boot time, use “rcctl enable radiusd”, which
     sets

           radiusd_flags=""

     in rc.conf.local(8).

     The options are as follows:

     --dd      Do not daemonize, log to stderr instead of syslog(3), and produce
             some additional debugging output.

     --ff _f_i_l_e
             Specify an alternative configuration file.

     --nn      Configtest mode.  Only check the configuration file for validity.

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/radiusd.conf    Default configuration file.

